● Reading the task now.

  The task is to fix createAsyncMemo so it:
  1. Deduplicates concurrent calls (one in-flight computation per key)
  2. Doesn't cache failures (rejects from cache, retries on next call)
  3. Caches successes (resolved values are reused)

  The bug in the original code is that it caches promises unconditionally—if a promise rejects, it stays cached, so retries get the same rejection.

  The fix: attach a rejection handler that removes the promise from cache on failure. On success, it stays cached.

  Let me write the solution and tests:

